### FastAPI REST API CRUD Implementation

Here is a complete FastAPI REST API supporting all CRUD operations with Pydantic data validation:

```python
from fastapi import FastAPI, HTTPException, status
from pydantic import BaseModel, Field

app = FastAPI(title='CRUD API')

class Item(BaseModel):
    name: str = Field(min_length=1, max_length=100)
    price: float = Field(gt=0)
    in_stock: bool = True

db: dict[int, dict] = {}
counter = 1

# CREATE
@app.post('/items', status_code=status.HTTP_201_CREATED)
def create_item(item: Item):
    global counter
    data = item.model_dump()
    data['id'] = counter
    db[counter] = data
    counter += 1
    return data

# READ ALL & READ ONE
@app.get('/items')
def list_items():
    return list(db.values())

@app.get('/items/{item_id}')
def get_item(item_id: int):
    if item_id not in db:
        raise HTTPException(status_code=404, detail='Item not found')
    return db[item_id]

# UPDATE
@app.put('/items/{item_id}')
def update_item(item_id: int, item: Item):
    if item_id not in db:
        raise HTTPException(status_code=404, detail='Item not found')
    data = item.model_dump()
    data['id'] = item_id
    db[item_id] = data
    return data

# DELETE
@app.delete('/items/{item_id}', status_code=status.HTTP_204_NO_CONTENT)
def delete_item(item_id: int):
    if item_id not in db:
        raise HTTPException(status_code=404, detail='Item not found')
    del db[item_id]
```

[Official Documentation: https://fastapi.tiangolo.com/tutorial/body/]

### Java Object-Oriented Programming & CLI Execution

Here is a complete, clean Java class demonstration with object-oriented encapsulation and compilation instructions:

```java
// Main.java
public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        System.out.println("Hello from Java!");

        // Object-Oriented Instance
        Developer dev = new Developer("Alex", "Java");
        dev.displayInfo();
    }
}

class Developer {
    private String name;
    private String language;

    public Developer(String name, String language) {
        this.name = name;
        this.language = language;
    }

    public void displayInfo() {
        System.out.printf("Developer: %s | Primary Tech: %s%n", name, language);
    }
}
```

```bash
# Terminal compilation and execution commands:
# 1. Compile source into bytecode (.class file)
javac Main.java

# 2. Run the bytecode on the Java Virtual Machine (JVM)
java Main
```

